WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:07.320
Just before we started today I mentioned that the mascot for the university, the tiger,

2
00:00:07.320 --> 00:00:14.680
came out of the Civil War brigades, Louisiana brigades, which were called the Louisiana Tigers.

3
00:00:14.680 --> 00:00:24.100
And that the first live mascot was in 1924, but the first tiger, I guess of the series that we have now was what, 1936?

4
00:00:24.100 --> 00:00:25.180
[agrees]

5
00:00:25.180 --> 00:00:26.540
Did you say the students bought him?

6
00:00:26.540 --> 00:00:27.160
Yeah.

7
00:00:27.160 --> 00:00:30.260
Contributed a dime apiece.

8
00:00:30.260 --> 00:00:36.820
It did say student contributions purchased a Bengal tiger named Sheik in 1936.

9
00:00:36.820 --> 00:00:38.960
The students contributed a dime apiece?

10
00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:39.520
[agrees]

11
00:00:39.520 --> 00:00:43.680
Nineteen thirty-six, they must have had what, how many students on campus?

12
00:00:43.680 --> 00:00:45.080
About five thousand, I would guess.

13
00:00:45.080 --> 00:00:46.995
Five thousand students, wasn’t that Oscar?

14
00:00:46.995 --> 00:00:48.420
Yeah, about.

15
00:00:48.420 --> 00:00:53.480
And that tiger was renamed for the football trainer named Mike Chambers.

16
00:00:53.480 --> 00:00:54.960
Yeah.

17
00:00:54.960 --> 00:00:56.200
What about Mike Chambers?

18
00:00:56.200 --> 00:00:58.360
Both of you apparently knew Mike Chambers.

19
00:00:58.360 --> 00:01:02.100
Well, he was a big guy.

20
00:01:02.100 --> 00:01:05.120
He had been . . . I think he was from the University of Illinois.

21
00:01:05.120 --> 00:01:07.440
I think he had played football with [Harold E.] “Red” Grange?

22
00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:07.900
Isn’t that right?

23
00:01:07.900 --> 00:01:09.400
[agrees] I think so.

24
00:01:09.400 --> 00:01:11.280
And he was a trainer for the U.S.

25
00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:14.160
Olympic team in 1932.

26
00:01:14.160 --> 00:01:17.740
And I think he came to LSU probably in ’34.

27
00:01:17.740 --> 00:01:19.300
I think [Coach Lawrence] “Biff” Jones brought him down.

28
00:01:19.300 --> 00:01:23.640
When Biff Jones became head coach, he brought him in as his trainer.

29
00:01:23.640 --> 00:01:27.080
Yeah, he was . . . He was pretty popular.

30
00:01:27.080 --> 00:01:30.040
And I think it was his idea to get a live mascot.

31
00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:31.220
Yeah.

32
00:01:31.220 --> 00:01:32.760
He instigated it.

33
00:01:32.760 --> 00:01:38.940
Tulane students stole the tiger one time, too, before a Tulane game.

34
00:01:38.940 --> 00:01:41.360
When was that Oscar?

35
00:01:41.360 --> 00:01:42.340
I don’t remember.

36
00:01:42.340 --> 00:01:44.160
Stole?

37
00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:44.780
They stole it, yeah.

38
00:01:44.780 --> 00:01:46.280
A big, a big tiger.

39
00:01:46.280 --> 00:01:47.680
Yeah, in his cage.

40
00:01:47.680 --> 00:01:48.580
Yeah.

41
00:01:48.580 --> 00:01:49.480
Oh, in his cage.

42
00:01:49.480 --> 00:01:59.980
Well, I recall in the late seventies when about two o’clock in the morning Campus Police called and said,

43
00:01:59.980 --> 00:02:05.560
“You know that Tiger is walking down Nicholson Drive.”

44
00:02:05.560 --> 00:02:05.760
And . . . actually,

45
00:02:05.660 --> 00:02:11.660
they said . . . no . . . “We got the . . . caught the tiger walking down Nicholson Drive.”

46
00:02:11.660 --> 00:02:17.440
And the fellow that . . . the cop is still on campus who did . . . who picked up the tiger.

47
00:02:17.440 --> 00:02:23.100
And he gradually got ahead of the tiger and just eased him and the tiger kind of turned and walked back.

48
00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:29.620
And another cop opened the gate to Bernie Moore Stadium and tiger went in there because there was bushes in there.

49
00:02:29.620 --> 00:02:34.740
And we called Bivin, Dr. Sheldon Bivin, who was our laboratory animal veterinarian.

50
00:02:34.740 --> 00:02:36.980
And he went out there with a capture gun,

51
00:02:36.980 --> 00:02:43.060
and he walked into Bernie Moore Stadium with that damn gun and darted that tiger and that’s how he got him back in the cage.

52
00:02:43.060 --> 00:02:46.150
But somebody had cut through the bolts and opened the doors.
